p:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Connection flange: according to make/[PERSON_129] offered,</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">including making the suitable branch/outlet in stainless steel pipeline DN 200 required for the installation of the safety valve and flange connection or tension-resistant pipe coupling, incl. all requred bolt, seal, other connecting material.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Make/[PERSON_129] offered overpressure/underpressure valve:</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/></Text><TextComplement MarkLbl="11" Kind="Bidder"><ComplCaption/><ComplBody><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">'.........................................................'</span></ComplBody><ComplTail><br/></ComplTail></TextComplement><Text><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">(e.g. Glogger or equivalent)</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">supply and assemble.</span></p></Text></DetailTxt><OutlineText><OutlTxt><TextOutlTxt><p style="width:481pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Overpressure/underpressure protection building</span></p></TextOutlTxt></OutlTxt></OutlineText></CompleteText></Description></Item><Item ID="id233" RNoPart="5"><Qty>1.000</Qty><QU>St</QU><Description><CompleteText><ComplTSB>Yes</ComplTSB><DetailTxt><Text><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Measuring device for flow - air</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Thermal mass flow meter</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">for installation in air-carrying pipelines; for direct mass flow measurement without additional pressure and temperature compensation; robust compact design</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><ul><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Measured medium air</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">Measuring range:	 </span><TextComplement MarkLbl="13" Kind="Bidder"><ComplBody><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">'......................'</span></ComplBody></TextComplement><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;"> (0 to 10000) Nm³/h</span></p></li></ul><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:48px 94px 141px 188px 236px 283px 330px 378px 424px 472px 519px 566px 613px 660px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">(planned nominal volume flow 800 Nm3/h)</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><ul><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">Pressure drop at full scale	 </span><TextComplement MarkLbl="14" Kind="Bidder"><ComplBody><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">'.......................'</span></ComplBody></TextComplement><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;"> mbar</span></p></li></ul><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><ul><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">fouling-resistant encapsulated sensor, response time 0,5 s</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Centring pin and connection flange for defined installation of the sensor in the pipeline</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Measurement deviation: 0,9% of reading +- 0,05% of full scale for air</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Reproducibility:			0,25 % of reading</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Ambient temperature:		5 to 25 °C</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Temperature measured medium:		10 to 25 °C</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Operating pressure at the measuring point: 	40 to 70 mbar(g)</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Degree of protection:				IP 65</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Current output:			4 to 20 mA</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Auxiliary power:				24 V DC (+-25%)</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Precision measurin section for maintaining the laminar flow profile; as precision fitting without edges and transitions (no risk of turbulence);</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Mounting adapter for aforementioned measuring device welded in radially for desired measuring accuracy with the following tolerances:</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">radial position of the measuring point of the probe +-0,5 mm</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">angular position of the mounting adapter +-0,2 degrees</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">with flange connection on both sides DIN EN1092-1 form A (matching the flanges of the continuing air pipes)</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Calibration measuring device with precision measurin section</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Special seals for minimising the annular gap</span></p></li></ul><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:47px 94px 141px 188px 236px 283px 330px 378px 424px 472px 519px 566px 613px 660px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">Nominal diameter:</span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">DN200</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:47px 94px 141px 188px 236px 283px 330px 378px 424px 472px 519px 566px 613px 660px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">Overall length:</span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">350 mm</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Manufacturer/supplier: 	 </span></p></Text><TextComplement MarkLbl="15" Kind="Bidder"><ComplCaption/><ComplBody><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">'............................................................'</span></ComplBody><ComplTail><br/></ComplTail></TextComplement><Text><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:47px 94px 141px 188px 236px 283px 330px 378px 424px 472px 519px 566px 613px 660px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">(e.g. GfW Gesellschaft für [FIRMA_068]</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:47px 94px 141px 188px 236px 283px 330px 378px 424px 472px 519px 566px 613px 660px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"></span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"></span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;"> or equivalent)</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/></Text><TextComplement MarkLbl="16" Kind="Bidder"><ComplCaption><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">[PERSON_129]:		 </span></ComplCaption><ComplBody><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">'....................................................................'</span></ComplBody><ComplTail><br/></ComplTail></TextComplement><Text><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:47px 94px 141px 188px 236px 283px 330px 378px 424px 472px 519px 566px 613px 660px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">(e.g. Airmaster DN 200 or equivalent)</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">In case of deviating manufacturer/[PERSON_129]/nominal diameter a data sheet with all relevant details (measuring range, measuring accuracy, connection nominal diameters, overall length, calming sections etc.) is to be enclosed with the bid.</span></p></Text></DetailTxt><OutlineText><OutlTxt><TextOutlTxt><p style="width:481pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Thermal air flow measurement</span></p></TextOutlTxt></OutlTxt></OutlineText></CompleteText></Description></Item></Itemlist></BoQBody></BoQCtgy><BoQCtgy ID="id234" RNoPart="03"><LblTx><p><span>[PERSON_110] feeder</span></p></LblTx><BoQBody><Itemlist><Item ID="id235" RNoPart="1"><Qty>1.000</Qty><QU>St</QU><Description><CompleteText><ComplTSB>Yes</ComplTSB><DetailTxt><Text><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Big Bag [PERSON_070] [PERSON_129] BBE-2.1</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">material [PERSON_115] drawing no. 58.00.00.00-R3,</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">for free-flowing bulk materials, in particular also for use in low rooms,</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">consisting of a robust steel frame, incl. lifting device. The lifting device is roller-mounted and equipped with an adjustable chains cone, which forms the Big Bag conically.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Triggering of the lifting device by gas springs on weight decrease in the Big Bag. Suitable for almost all Big Bag sizes.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">For Big Bags dimension: up to approx. 120 cm x 100 cm (B x L), </span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Total height: approx. 1190 mm </span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Gas spring stroke: approx. 350 mm </span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Frame material: [PERSON_115] 1.4301</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Surface: glass bead blasted</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Including maintenance-free cable iris dosing valve,  [PERSON_129] BIDV-7.1-S-S, long version, with manual operation and re-locking.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">(The re-locking automatically turns the valve further closed by means of integrated gas springs when material settles in the Big Bag outlet). </span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">The valve rotary unit consists of a Roller-guided  slewing ring with glass-fibre-stabilised stainless steel cable arcs, plastic-reinforced, which are arranged Iris-shaped. The hand lever turns by 180° and is recessed in the frame profile in the end positions.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Valve base housing: material 1.4301</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Valve mechanism: material 1.4301 except bearings</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Valve rotary unit: material 1.4301</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">The mechanism of the valve is maintenance-free. Functions directly at the Big Bag outlet: closing product grain size smaller than 5 µm, dosing, to re-tie (partially emptied Big Bags can thereby be taken out again).</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;"><span style="font-size:10pt;text-decoration:underline ;font-family:Arial;">Including 1 piece sub-platform </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">for [PERSON_070],</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">executed as robust stainless steel frame, foot design steel plates with fastening holes. The [PERSON_070] is U-shaped open towards the front side.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Material: [PERSON_115] 1.4301</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Surface: glass bead blasted</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Installation height: approx. 1200 mm - to be adapted to local conditions: before ordering coordination with lifting gear to be supplied by others on site required!.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/></Text><TextComplement MarkLbl="11" Kind="Bidder"><ComplCaption><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Supplier/manufacturer:	 </span></ComplCaption><ComplBody><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">'......................................................'</span></ComplBody><ComplTail><br/></ComplTail></TextComplement><Text><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:18px 37px 75px 113px 151px 189px 226px 264px 302px 340px 378px 415px 453px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">(e.g. BIG BAG SYSTEMS, [ORT_015]</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:18px 37px 75px 113px 151px 189px 226px 264px 302px 340px 378px 415px 453px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;"> or equivalent)</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/></Text><TextComplement MarkLbl="12" Kind="Bidder"><ComplCaption><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">[PERSON_129]:				 </span></ComplCaption><ComplBody><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">'......................................................'</span></ComplBody><ComplTail><br/></ComplTail></TextComplement><Text><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:18px 37px 75px 113px 151px 189px 226px 264px 302px 340px 378px 415px 453px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">(e.g. [PERSON_129] BBE-2.1 or equivalent)</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Supply and assemble ready for operation.</span></p></Text></DetailTxt><OutlineText><OutlTxt><TextOutlTxt><p style="width:481pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">[PERSON_070]</span></p></TextOutlTxt></OutlTxt></OutlineText></CompleteText></Description></Item><Item ID="id236" RNoPart="2"><Qty>1.000</Qty><QU>St</QU><Description><CompleteText><ComplTSB>Yes</ComplTSB><DetailTxt><Text><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Liquid jet solids pump</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">of CrNi-[PERSON_089], stationary,</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:18px 37px 75px 113px 151px 189px 226px 264px 302px 340px 378px 415px 453px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">Supplier/manufacturer:</span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">[FIRMA_022] or equivalent</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Type: FFeP of CrNi-[PERSON_089] (stationary), order number 181001 473195 or equivalent</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/></Text><TextComplement MarkLbl="11" Kind="Bidder"><ComplCaption><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Make offered:	 </span></ComplCaption><ComplBody><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">'.....................................................'</span></ComplBody><ComplTail><br/></ComplTail></TextComplement><Text><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/></Text><TextComplement MarkLbl="12" Kind="Bidder"><ComplCaption><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">[PERSON_129] offered:		 </span></ComplCaption><ComplBody><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">'.....................................................'</span></ComplBody><ComplTail><br/></ComplTail></TextComplement><Text><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Supply and install ready for operation.</span></p></Text></DetailTxt><OutlineText><OutlTxt><TextOutlTxt><p style="width:481pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Liquid jet solids pump</span></p></TextOutlTxt></OutlTxt></OutlineText></CompleteText></Description></Item></Itemlist></BoQBody></BoQCtgy><BoQCtgy ID="id237" RNoPart="04"><LblTx><p><span>Temporary deacidification plant</span></p></LblTx><BoQBody><Itemlist><Item ID="id238" RNoPart="1"><LumpSumItem>Yes</LumpSumItem><Qty>1.000</Qty><QU>psch</QU><Description><CompleteText><ComplTSB>Yes</ComplTSB><DetailTxt><Text><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Water jet ventilator for deacidification and oxygen enrichment of raw well water,</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:18px 37px 75px 113px 151px 189px 226px 264px 302px 340px 378px 415px 453px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">Design throughput:</span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">60 m³/h </span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Liquid jet ventilator DN 150, </span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">with the following connections: </span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:18px 37px 75px 113px 151px 189px 226px 264px 302px 340px 378px 415px 453px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">Suction side [PERSON_060]:</span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">DN 80, </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">PN 16 (lateral)</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:18px 37px 75px 113px 151px 189px 226px 264px 302px 340px 378px 415px 453px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">Motive water side:</span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">DN 100,</span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">PN 16 (axial)</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:18px 37px 75px 113px 151px 189px 226px 264px 302px 340px 378px 415px 453px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">Mixtures outlet:</span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">DN 150,</span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">PN 10 (loose flange of 1.4541)</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Dimensions: </span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:18px 37px 75px 113px 151px 189px 226px 264px 302px 340px 378px 415px 453px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">Total length:</span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">approx. 1.680 mm</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Between motive side and</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:18px 37px 75px 113px 151px 189px 226px 264px 302px 340px 378px 415px 453px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">mixture outlet:</span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">approx. 1.500 mm</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Weight: approx. 50 kg</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Design:  </span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Head, mixing section and diffuser completely welded of CrNi-[PERSON_089] 1.4571. </span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Replaceable motive nozzle system likewise of CrNi-[PERSON_089] 1.4571/81.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Including annular throttle valve DN 80 of CrNi-[PERSON_089], which is assembled between suction side and the counter flange of the continuing pipeline.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Performance data at the design point (with reference to the connections):</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:18px 37px 75px 113px 151px 189px 226px 264px 302px 340px 378px 415px 453px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">Suction flow:</span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">120 Nm³/h [PERSON_060] </span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:18px 37px 75px 113px 151px 189px 226px 264px 302px 340px 378px 415px 453px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">Suction flow temperature:</span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">20 °C</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:18px 37px 75px 113px 151px 189px 226px 264px 302px 340px 378px 415px 453px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">Suction pressure:</span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">995 mbar abs. = minus 50 mmWs </span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">(pressure loss for air filter and throttle valve)</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:18px 37px 75px 113px 151px 189px 226px 264px 302px 340px 378px 415px 453px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">Motive flow:</span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">60 m³/h water</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:18px 37px 75px 113px 151px 189px 226px 264px 302px 340px 378px 415px 453px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">Motive water pressure:</span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">1,8 bar abs. = 8 mWS </span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:18px 37px 75px 113px 151px 189px 226px 264px 302px 340px 378px 415px 453px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">Mixture outlet:</span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">1,030 bar abs. = +300 mmWS </span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Achievable degree of deacidification: 60 % </span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Installation position: </span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Vertical with water flow from top to bottom. A downstream downpipe may be max. 300 mm long and must be laid in the connection nominal diameter of the jet pump. It can be submerged max. 300mm below the water level.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Design basis: </span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">The pressure-bearing components of the liquid jet ventilator are designed for:</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:18px 37px 75px 113px 151px 189px 226px 264px 302px 340px 378px 415px 453px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">Housing:</span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">min./max. permissible pressure PS: -0,5/+0,5 bar</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:18px 37px 75px 113px 151px 189px 226px 264px 302px 340px 378px 415px 453px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">min./max. permissible temperature TS: 5/30 °C </span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:18px 37px 75px 113px 151px 189px 226px 264px 302px 340px 378px 415px 453px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">Motive nozzle:</span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">max. permissible pressure PS: 2 bar</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:18px 37px 75px 113px 151px 189px 226px 264px 302px 340px 378px 415px 453px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">min./max. permissible temperature TS: 5/30 °C </span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Calculation code: AD-2000</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Classification acc. to Directive 2014/68/EU: </span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">With classification acc. to Directive 2014/68/EU, fluid group 2, medium state liquid or gaseous, it follows from Article 4, paragraph (3), that only sound engineering practice has to be applied. A CE mark must not be affixed.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Including documentation, to be submitted in pdf format (see also separate item in the division "Site setup and documentation"):</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><ul><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">binding drawing,</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Installation and operating instructions </span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Certificates in the form described below</span></p></li></ul><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Including factory acceptance, consisting of internal construction inspection as well as a hydrostatic pressure test, incl. works test certificate with confirmation of:</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><ul><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Specified material </span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Compliance with relevant dimensions </span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Visual inspection </span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Hydrostatic pressure test</span></p></li></ul><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Manufacturer/supplier</span></p></Text><TextComplement MarkLbl="11" Kind="Bidder"><ComplCaption><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">and size:	 </span></ComplCaption><ComplBody><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">'..................................................................'</span></ComplBody><ComplTail><br/></ComplTail></TextComplement><Text><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:18px 37px 75px 113px 151px 189px 226px 264px 302px 340px 378px 415px 453px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">(e. [FIRMA_090], DN 150 / 60 m3/h</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:18px 37px 75px 113px 151px 189px 226px 264px 302px 340px 378px 415px 453px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">or equivalent)</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Supply and assemble ready for operation, incl. all required fastening material and commissioning as part of the overall commissioning.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/></Text></DetailTxt><OutlineText><OutlTxt><TextOutlTxt><p style="width:481pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Water jet ventilator 60 m3/h</span></p></TextOutlTxt></OutlTxt></OutlineText></CompleteText></Description></Item></Itemlist></BoQBody></BoQCtgy><BoQCtgy ID="id239" RNoPart="05"><LblTx><p><span>Equipment arsenic removal filter</span></p></LblTx><BoQBody><Itemlist><Item ID="id240" RNoPart="1"><Qty>2.000</Qty><QU>St</QU><Description><CompleteText><ComplTSB>Yes</ComplTSB><DetailTxt><Text><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Remove and dispose of filter nozzles in existing open filter basin - area per filter floor 5,9 m2, number of nozzles approx. 410 pieces.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Install new filter nozzles in the following design:</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Cushion pipe nozzles, air slot in the cushion pipe burr-free and at least 2 mm wide; burr-free "working bore" arranged above the slot with at least 2 mm diameter; with the possibility of a height compensation of at least 5 mm;</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Number of nozzles approx 410 pieces / filter</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">(70 pieces per m2)</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/></Text><TextComplement MarkLbl="11" Kind="Bidder"><ComplCaption><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Nozzle make:	</span></ComplCaption><ComplBody><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">'........................'</span></ComplBody><ComplTail><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;"> (e.g. KSH)</span><br/></ComplTail></TextComplement><Text><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/></Text><TextComplement MarkLbl="12" Kind="Bidder"><ComplCaption><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Nozzle type:	</span></ComplCaption><ComplBody><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">'........................'</span></ComplBody><ComplTail><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;"> (e.g. [PERSON_129] S3 or equivalent)</span><br/></ComplTail></TextComplement><Text><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Attention: nozzles may only be assembled after approval by site management! The final determination of the filter nozzles can only be made after removal of the filter material in the open filters and ascertainment of the existing condition.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Price supply and assemble per filter</span></p></Text></DetailTxt><OutlineText><OutlTxt><TextOutlTxt><p style="width:481pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Renewal filter nozzles (incl. removal of existing nozzles)</span></p></TextOutlTxt></OutlTxt></OutlineText></CompleteText></Description></Item><Item ID="id241" RNoPart="2"><Qty>2.000</Qty><QU>St</QU><Description><CompleteText><ComplTSB>Yes</ComplTSB><DetailTxt><Text><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Supply and install support and filter layers for open arsenic removal filter:</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">The arsenic removal filters each have a base area of around 6,0 m2.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Support layer:</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">[PERSON_005] of washed and fire-dried quartz gravel acc. to DIN 12904,</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">grain size 2,00-3,15 mm</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Height of the [PERSON_005] 30 cm (1,8 m3 bulk volume installed)</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/></Text><TextComplement MarkLbl="11" Kind="Bidder"><ComplCaption><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Supplying company:	</span></ComplCaption><ComplBody><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">'.................................................'</span></ComplBody><ComplTail><br/></ComplTail></TextComplement><Text><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:48px 96px 144px 192px 240px 288px 336px 384px 432px 480px 529px 576px 624px 672px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">(e.g. Amberger Kaolinwerke)</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Filter layer:</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">[PERSON_058] GEH 102</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:48px 96px 144px 192px 240px 288px 336px 384px 432px 480px 529px 576px 624px 672px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">Manufacturer:</span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">[FIRMA_032]</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:48px 96px 144px 192px 240px 288px 336px 384px 432px 480px 529px 576px 624px 672px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">49090 Osnabrück</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:48px 96px 144px 192px 240px 288px 336px 384px 432px 480px 529px 576px 624px 672px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">Installed quantity per filter:</span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">8.300 kg</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:48px 96px 144px 192px 240px 288px 336px 384px 432px 480px 529px 576px 624px 672px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">corresponds to a layer height of:</span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">1,20 m</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">The material quantity per arsenic removal filter corresponds to a delivery quantity of 10 Big Bags of 830 kg each.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">The layers must without fail be placed separately one after the other!</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">When placing support and filter layers the manufacturer's instructions for filling, installation flushing and disinfection are to be observed:</span></p><ul><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Partial filling of the filter basin with [PERSON_029] to avoid damage to the filter nozzles</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Place, level and flush quartz gravel acc. to DIN 12904 as [PERSON_005] according to the manufacturer's specifications</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Hydraulic placement of the GEH® by means of injector system and motive water</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Installation flushing in upflow to remove the fines from the adsorber bed, backwash velocity 26 m/h; flushing until the outflow water is free of turbidity (approx. 15 minutes)</span></p></li></ul><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Delivery is in Big Bags. Installation is carried out using the feeding system of motive pump and Big Bag emptying system likewise contained in the scope of this bill of quantities.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">For the period of placing the filter fillings it is to be assumed for the cost estimate that no valves are yet electrically connected, i.e. corresponding time expenditure for manual local operation of the plant is to be included in the price and is not paid separately.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Supply support and filter layers completely and install professionally for 1 filter</span></p></Text></DetailTxt><OutlineText><OutlTxt><TextOutlTxt><p style="width:481pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Filter filling arsenic removal filter</span></p></TextOutlTxt></OutlTxt></OutlineText></CompleteText></Description></Item><Item ID="id242" RNoPart="3"><Qty>2.000</Qty><QU>St</QU><Description><CompleteText><DetailTxt><Text><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">After completion of the installation flushing a separate disinfection of the open arsenic removal filters with hydrogen peroxide acc. to manufacturer's recommendation GEH® is to be carried out.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">The disinfectant, e.g. 1 container Veolia Hydrex 9561 per filter, is to be introduced into the filter.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">After a contact time of at least 2 hours a disinfection flushing in upflow to remove the [PERSON_029] charged with disinfectant from the adsorber bed, backwash velocity 26 m/h, will to be carried out; flushing until the outflow water is free of turbidity and for Multiple water exchange in the filter bed, duration at least 10 minutes.</span></p></Text></DetailTxt><OutlineText><OutlTxt><TextOutlTxt><p style="width:481pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Disinfection arsenic removal filter</span></p></TextOutlTxt></OutlTxt></OutlineText></CompleteText></Description></Item><Item ID="id243" RNoPart="4"><Qty>2.000</Qty><QU>St</QU><Description><CompleteText><DetailTxt><Text><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Overflow channels of [PERSON_115] are installed in the open filter basins.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Length of the channel: around 3,0 m</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Photo of the channel see construction description (Fig. 5 and 7).</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">The channel is to be dismantled in the course of the dismantling work, carefully packed in foil and stored for reassembly.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">After completion of the structural refurbishment / before placing the new filter material the channel is to be assembled into the filter basin again.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Dismantling, protection, intermediate transport on the site, reassembly of the overflow channel incl. new fastening material. Billing per filter basin.</span></p></Text></DetailTxt><OutlineText><OutlTxt><TextOutlTxt><p style="width:481pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Dismantling and reassembly overflow channel filter basin</span></p></TextOutlTxt></OutlTxt></OutlineText></CompleteText></Description></Item><Item ID="id244" RNoPart="5"><Qty>2.000</Qty><QU>St</QU><Description><CompleteText><DetailTxt><Text><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Press-fitting pipelines DN 50 for the filter floor venting are installed in the open filter basins.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Length of the lines around 5 m</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Photo of the line (as far as visible) see construction description (Fig. 5 and 7).</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">The pipeline including solenoid valve is to be dismantled and packed in foil.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">After completion of the structural refurbishment / before placing the new filter material the pipeline is to be disinfected and assembled into the filter basin again.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Dismantling, protection, intermediate transport on the site, reassembly of the filter floor venting line with installed solenoid valve, incl. new fastening material/pipe supports, billing per filter basin.</span></p></Text></DetailTxt><OutlineText><OutlTxt><TextOutlTxt><p style="width:481pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Dismantling and reassembly filter floor venting filter basin</span></p></TextOutlTxt></OutlTxt></OutlineText></CompleteText></Description></Item></Itemlist></BoQBody></BoQCtgy></BoQBody></BoQCtgy><BoQCtgy ID="id245" RNoPart="04"><LblTx><p><span>Measuring devices</span></p></LblTx><BoQBody><BoQCtgy ID="id246" RNoPart="01"><LblTx><p><span>Flow meters for liquids</span></p></LblTx><BoQBody><Itemlist><Item ID="id247" RNoPart="1"><Qty>6.000</Qty><QU>St</QU><Description><CompleteText><ComplTSB>Yes</ComplTSB><DetailTxt><Text><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Electromagnetic flow meter as flange version:</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">suitable for use with drinking water</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><ul><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Nominal diameter DN 100</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Pressure rating PN 16</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Lining PP</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Process connection: flange acc. to EN 1092-1, PN16</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Design: compact version</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Measuring accuracy: deviation max. +/- 0,5 % of the measured value</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">with operating display</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Certificate: drinking water approvals KTW, DVGW</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Measuring range freely Adjustable</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Field housing sheet steel</span></p></li></ul><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Electrical, instrumentation and control characteristics:</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><ul><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Voltage 230 V, 50 Hz</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Outputs: current /pulse and switching outputs</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Degree of protection IP 67</span></p></li></ul><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Make / [PERSON_129]: [FIRMA_059] OPTIFLUX 2050 or equivalent</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">To be stated by the bidder, if deviating from the above specifications or the qualities of the reference make:</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><ul><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">Lining:			 </span><TextComplement MarkLbl="14" Kind="Bidder"><ComplBody><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">'................'</span></ComplBody></TextComplement><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;"> </span></p></li></ul><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><ul><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">Electrodes: material no.:	 </span><TextComplement MarkLbl="15" Kind="Bidder"><ComplBody><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">'................ '</span></ComplBody></TextComplement><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;"> </span></p></li></ul><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><ul><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">Calibration:			 </span><TextComplement MarkLbl="16" Kind="Bidder"><ComplBody><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">'................ '</span></ComplBody></TextComplement><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;"> </span></p></li></ul><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/></Text><TextComplement MarkLbl="17" Kind="Bidder"><ComplCaption><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Make/ [PERSON_129]: </span></ComplCaption><ComplBody><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">'......................................................'</span></ComplBody><ComplTail><br/></ComplTail></TextComplement><Text><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">supply and assemble ready for operation</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/></Text></DetailTxt><OutlineText><OutlTxt><TextOutlTxt><p style="width:481pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Magnetic-inductive flow measurement DN 100</span></p></TextOutlTxt></OutlTxt></OutlineText></CompleteText></Description></Item></Itemlist></BoQBody></BoQCtgy><BoQCtgy ID="id248" RNoPart="02"><LblTx><p><span>Pressure measuring devices</span></p></LblTx><BoQBody><Itemlist><Item ID="id249" RNoPart="1"><Qty>6.000</Qty><QU>St</QU><Description><CompleteText><ComplTSB>Yes</ComplTSB><DetailTxt><Text><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Bourdon tube glycerine pressure gauge</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">for installation in pipelines carrying [PERSON_060] or drinking water.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Housing, bayonet ring, pressure connection and pointer mechanism, completely of CrNi-[PERSON_089] ([PERSON_176]), dial aluminium white, scale [PERSON_031], pointer in aluminium, black</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:48px 96px 144px 192px 240px 288px 336px 384px 432px 480px 529px 576px 624px 672px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">Display diameter:</span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">100 mm</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:48px 96px 144px 192px 240px 288px 336px 384px 432px 480px 529px 576px 624px 672px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">Filling liquid:</span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">glycerine</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:48px 96px 144px 192px 240px 288px 336px 384px 432px 480px 529px 576px 624px 672px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">Measuring accuracy:</span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">min. class 1,0</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:48px 96px 144px 192px 240px 288px 336px 384px 432px 480px 529px 576px 624px 672px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">Measuring range:</span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">0 - 1,0 bar</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/></Text><TextComplement MarkLbl="11" Kind="Bidder"><ComplCaption><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Make:		</span></ComplCaption><ComplBody><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">'........................................'</span></ComplBody><ComplTail><br/></ComplTail></TextComplement><Text><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:48px 96px 144px 192px 240px 288px 336px 384px 432px 480px 529px 576px 624px 672px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">(Wika or equivalent)</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/></Text><TextComplement MarkLbl="12" Kind="Bidder"><ComplCaption><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">[PERSON_129]:			</span></ComplCaption><ComplBody><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">'.......................................'</span></ComplBody><ComplTail><br/></ComplTail></TextComplement><Text><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;font-family:Arial;">Pressure gauge valve</span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;"> with test flange 1/2 inch see </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;font-family:Arial;">separate item.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">supply and assemble.</span></p></Text></DetailTxt><OutlineText><OutlTxt><TextOutlTxt><p style="width:481pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Pressure gauge up to 1 bar</span></p></TextOutlTxt></OutlTxt></OutlineText></CompleteText></Description></Item><Item ID="id250" RNoPart="2"><Qty>5.000</Qty><QU>St</QU><Description><CompleteText><DetailTxt><Text><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Bourdon tube glycerine pressure gauge</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">for installation in pipelines carrying [PERSON_060] or drinking water.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;tab-stops:48px 96px 144px 192px 240px 288px 336px 384px 432px 480px 529px 576px 624px 672px;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">Measuring range:</span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;mso-tab-count:1;font-family:Arial;"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">0 - 3 bar,</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">otherwise as before</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;font-family:Arial;">Pressure gauge valve</span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;"> with test flange 1/2 inch </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;font-family:Arial;">see separate item.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">supply and assemble.</span></p></Text></DetailTxt><OutlineText><OutlTxt><TextOutlTxt><p style="width:481pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Pressure gauge up to 3 bar</span></p></TextOutlTxt></OutlTxt></OutlineText></CompleteText></Description></Item></Itemlist></BoQBody></BoQCtgy></BoQBody></BoQCtgy><BoQCtgy ID="id251" RNoPart="05"><LblTx><p><span>Pipelines</span></p></LblTx><BoQBody><BoQCtgy ID="id252" RNoPart="01"><LblTx><p><span>Pipelines made of stainless [PERSON_089]</span></p></LblTx><BoQBody><Itemlist><Remark ID="id253"><Description><CompleteText><DetailTxt><Text><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Pipelines made of stainless steel</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">General rules for execution:</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">The requirements and designs listed below are to be complied with and to be included in the price of the respective pipeline items.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Connection points:</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">All connection points (position, dimension) are to be surveyed exactly on site. The information in the tender documents does not release the bidder from this obligation. Subsequent claims based on failure to carry out the survey are not accepted.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Venting / air admission and drains</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Unless otherwise required, venting / air admission facilities are to be provided at unavoidable high points of pipelines carrying liquid and drain facilities at low points.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Pipe connections</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">All pipelines must be connected to each other and to the vessels, wall penetrations, valves, measuring devices etc. with easily detachable screwed, clamp or compression connections or, for nominal diameters &gt; DN 50, exclusively with flange connections. For connections of different metallic materials (e.g. filter vessel - stainless steel line, but also components with non-conductive external corrosion protection, e.g. EKB) including supports, clamps etc., an electrical separation "insulating flange" is to be provided to prevent contact corrosion.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Surcharges to the usual flange connections of the nominal diameters to be offered in this LV for producing an electrical separation point at a flange connection to avoid corrosion consisting of:</span></p><ul><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">in piece insulating flange gasket,</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Insulating sleeves, one piece per hole</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Insulating washers, two pieces per hole</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Steel washers, two pieces per hole</span></p></li></ul><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">are to be included in the unit prices of the valves to be installed.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">For electrical consumers (valves,measuring devices etc.) installed in stainless steel pipelines, earthing lugs for connecting an earthing cable connection by others on site must in addition be welded onto the adjoining stainless steel pipeline parts.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Pipelines carrying drinking water from DN 65 and larger, in flange-saving design, incl. all necessary components (e.g. weld-on flanges etc.) welding consumables and auxiliary materials,</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">in particular in compliance with the following specification:</span></p><ul><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">permissible component size max. fitting length 5.000 mm</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">max. fitting width for outlets and bends 1.500 mm</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Material: all pipes, bends, reducers and flanges in material number 1.4571</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Pipes: longitudinally welded and pickled round pipes  v = 1,0, DIN EN 10216-5.</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">The minimum wall thickness of the pipes is to be designed according to the max. occurring operating pressures acc. to AD-Merkblatt B0 and B1 and the structural requirements, whereby the max. deflection of the pipeline in the ready-for-operation state is fixed at one four-hundredth of the span. A structural proof is to be provided at the request of site management.</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">If the requirements from structural analysis or welded connections result in smaller wall thicknesses, at least the following wall thicknesses are nevertheless to be complied with:</span></p><ul><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">DN 10 - 32:	2,0 mm</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">DN 40 - 80:	2,0 mm</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">DN 100 - 150:	2,6 mm</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">DN 200:	2,9 mm</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">DN 250:	3,0 mm</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">DN 300 - 350:	3,2 mm</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">DN 400 - 500:	4,0 mm</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">DN 600 - 1000:	5,0 mm</span></p></li></ul></li></ul><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><ul><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Bends: longitudinally welded and pickled bends type 3; from DN 400 R = d + 100</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Reducers: longitudinally welded and pickled reducers; overall length according to DIN EN 10253; minimum wall thickness according to pipe wall thickness</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Flanges: acc. to DIN EN 1092-1</span></p></li></ul><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Requirements for the workshop producing the pipelines:</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">All fittings are to be fabricated in the works ready for assembly in ferrite-free rooms. Fabrication in rooms in which ferritic steels are also processed is not permitted.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">In addition, only ferrite-free tools and lifting gear may be used for processing the fittings. The ferrite-free fabrication is agreed not as an ancillary service but as a main service.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Site welds are permitted only in exceptional cases and only with the express approval of site management. With the bid, the specialist pipeline company is to be named and proof of its ferrite-free fabrication is to be submitted.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Fusion welding processes</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">For welding processes for the aforementioned fittings, exclusively the individual processes acc. to ISO 4063 13 gas-shielded metal arc welding 14 gas-shielded tungsten arc welding are permitted. The material with the number 1.4576 is to be used as welding filler material.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Weld seam quality</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">As minimum requirements the quality level for imperfections EN DIN 5817 group D applies with the exception of reference no. 2017 (acc. to ISO 6520-1). For this reference number EN DIN 5817 group B applies as minimum requirement.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Quality assurance</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">For quality assurance of the weld seams a non-destructive test acc. to ISO 17637 is carried out. This test can be carried out by site management or by an independent expert separately commissioned by the building owner during and after fabrication of the fittings. Should there be disagreement between the AN and site management or the expert about the quality assessment, the AG can additionally order a radiographic test.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Post-treatment of the fittings</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">All pipe fittings are to be pickled and passivated in a full immersion bath after welding. For transport to the site all openings of the fittings are to be closed with covers and packed in suitable fabric-reinforced film at least 0,5 mm thick.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Assembly of the fittings</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">The fittings are to be delivered to the site free of damage.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">For moving and assembling the fittings no ferritic tools may be used on site. Only stainless steels, plastics or fabric slings are permitted. If ferritic contamination is found after assembly, the pipes and fittings concerned are to be removed and pickled and passivated in a full immersion bath in the works at the expense of the party responsible. To ensure a nearly stress-free assembly, all pipe supports are to be made height-adjustable.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Before acceptance, in coordination with site management, all films are to be removed, the pipelines given a final cleaning and oiled with an agent suitable for drinking water.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">General notes on the piping are also to be observed.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Flanges: </span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;"><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;">The use of flanges PN 10 (acc. to EN 1092-1:2018-1) with </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;font-family:Arial;">reduced flange plate thickness</span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;"> is generally permitted if, for the nominal diameters tendered, the tightness of the pipe connection is proven by calculation acc. to AD-Merkblatt (calculation is to be enclosed with the bid)</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Flange bolts / nuts:</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Bolts and washers: min. 1.4401; nuts: min. 1.4571</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Reducers:</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Eccentric or concentric design according to the technical requirements in the pipe system, wall thicknesses and other requirements as above.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Saddle nozzles:</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">[PERSON_129]: made from pipe bend. Wall thicknesses and other requirements as above.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Adjusting and dismantling pieces:</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">All spindles and nuts of 1.4571. All sealing elements of material approved to KTW and DVGW W270. Wall thicknesses and other requirements as above.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Pipe support and pipe holders:</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Height-adjustable steel section constructions for support, [PERSON_074], hanging and special fixings including fixing material such as anchors or stainless steel screws. The supports / suspensions must be designed so that all loads occurring in operation are safely absorbed.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">The pipes are to be installed by means of 2-part flat steel pipe clamps with PVC insert.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">The supports are to be protected with suitable protective film until acceptance of the plant.</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">ALL VALVES AND OTHER MACHINES AND DEVICES ARE TO BE ASSEMBLED STRESS-FREE IN COMPLIANCE WITH MANUFACTURER'S INSTRUCTIONS (for example regarding calming sections)!</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Billing notes:</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><ul><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Unless expressly stated otherwise in the item text, the SUPPLY AND ASSEMBLY READY FOR OPERATION IS TO BE INCLUDED IN THE PRICE in the unit prices for the pipeline, fitting and pipeline accessory items.</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">The billing length of the stainless steel pipelines is determined incl. the flanges and fittings, etc., machines (e.g. pumps, blowers), valves and filter housings (air filtration) are however not measured through. In this respect the flanges and fittings are to be priced as SURCHARGE TO THE RESPECTIVE PIPELINE with corresponding nominal diameter.</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">WELD SEAMS are not paid separately. They are TO BE INCLUDED IN THE PRICE of the items of the fittings and flanges.</span></p></li><li><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Flange connection sets (bolts, washers, gaskets and - where required - galvanic separation) are TO BE INCLUDED IN THE PRICE of the items of the flanges or valves.</span></p></li></ul></Text></DetailTxt><OutlineText><OutlTxt><TextOutlTxt><p style="width:481pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Specification pipelines</span></p></TextOutlTxt></OutlTxt></OutlineText></CompleteText></Description></Remark><Item ID="id254" RNoPart="1"><Qty>20.000</Qty><QU>m</QU><Description><CompleteText><DetailTxt><Text><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Stainless steel pipe DN 65, up to PN 16</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Pressure pipe acc. to preliminary remark pipelines,</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:284pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">76,1 x 2,0 mm</span></p></Text></DetailTxt><OutlineText><OutlTxt><TextOutlTxt><p style="width:481pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Stainless steel pipe DN 65</span></p></TextOutlTxt></OutlTxt></OutlineText></CompleteText></Description></Item><Item ID="id255" RNoPart="2"><Qty>5.000</Qty><QU>m</QU><Description><CompleteText><DetailTxt><Text><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:397pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Stainless steel pipe DN 80, up to PN 16</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:397pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:397pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Pressure pipe acc. to preliminary remark pipelines,</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:397pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">88,9 x 2,0 mm</span></p></Text></DetailTxt><OutlineText><OutlTxt><TextOutlTxt><p style="width:481pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Stainless steel pipe DN 80</span></p></TextOutlTxt></OutlTxt></OutlineText></CompleteText></Description></Item><Item ID="id256" RNoPart="3"><Qty>25.000</Qty><QU>m</QU><Description><CompleteText><DetailTxt><Text><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:397pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Stainless steel pipe DN 100, up to PN 16</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:397pt;font-size:10pt;"/><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:397pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">Pressure pipe acc. to preliminary remark pipelines,</span></p><p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;width:397pt;font-size:10pt;"><span style="font-family:Arial;font-size:10pt;">114,3 x 2,6 mm</span></p></Text></DetailTxt><OutlineText><OutlTxt><TextOutlTxt><p style="width:481pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt;"><span